/1551152/000155115225000020/abbv-20241231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "ABBV_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0018", "ticker": "ABBV", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2024", "period_end": "2024-12-31", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 1.4904, "filing_name": "AbbVie Inc 10-K FY2024", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1551152/000155115225000020/abbv-20241231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "ABBV_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0022", "ticker": "ABBV", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2024", "period_end": "2024-12-31", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 1.487, "filing_name": "AbbVie Inc 10-K FY2024", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1551152/000155115225000020/abbv-20241231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "ABBV_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0017", "ticker": "ABBV", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2024", "period_end": "2024-12-31", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 1.4869, "filing_name": "AbbVie Inc 10-K FY2024", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1551152/000155115225000020/abbv-20241231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "ABBV_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0027", "ticker": "ABBV", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2024", "period_end": "2024-12-31", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 0.029, "filing_name": "AbbVie Inc 10-K FY2024", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1551152/000155115225000020/abbv-20241231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "ABBV_10K_2024-12-31__business__0038", "ticker": "ABBV", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2024", "period_end": "2024-12-31", "section": "business", "score": 0.9272, "filing_name": "AbbVie Inc 10-K FY2024", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1551152/000155115225000020/abbv-20241231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "ABBV_10K_2024-12-31__business__0032", "ticker": "ABBV", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2024", "period_end": "2024-12-31", "section": "business", "score": 0.9056, "filing_name": "AbbVie Inc 10-K FY2024", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1551152/000155115225000020/abbv-20241231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "ABBV_10K_2024-12-31__business__0033", "ticker": "ABBV", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2024", "period_end": "2024-12-31", "section": "business", "score": 0.8664, "filing_name": "AbbVie Inc 10-K FY2024", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1551152/000155115225000020/abbv-20241231.htm", "truncated": false}], "collapsed_near_duplicates": 88, "dropped_candidates": 784, "token_estimate": 31947, "gaps": [], "degraded": []}, "answer": {"direct_answer": "All five companies describe regulatory risk in three areas: drug pricing and reimbursement, approval and post-approval oversight, and compliance enforcement. Pfizer cites the IRA and state price-limiting measures [PFE_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0016], and J&J says the IRA subjects some products to government-set pricing beginning in 2026 [JNJ_10K_2025-12-28__risk_factors__0004]. Merck and AbbVie describe FDA/HHS policy change risk and post-approval compliance exposure [MRK_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0028] [ABBV_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0022], while Lilly cites changing U.S. enforcement priorities and cGMP scrutiny [LLY_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0037]. On responses, the chunks show Lilly investing in company-wide quality systems and cGMP compliance [LLY_10K_2025-12-31__business__0074], Merck engaging in public policy advocacy on cost containment [MRK_10K_2024-12-31__business__0022], and AbbVie incurring expense and effort to comply [ABBV_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0022]. Pfizer reports that its 2018 Corporate Integrity Agreement was closed by the OIG in January 2025 [PFE_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0024]. Several risk passages state no specific response, and Keel does not give advice or rank these risks.", "company_findings": [{"ticker": "PFE", "company": "Pfizer Inc", "findings": [{"point": "Pfizer faces pricing regulation risk from the IRA, state drug affordability boards, and foreign government payors such as China's VBP process (10-K for fiscal 2024, ended December 31, 2024).", "citations": ["PFE_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0016"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Regulatory approvals can be affected by differing interpretations of data, accelerated approval contingencies, and post-marketing study results, with possible label changes or loss of approval.", "citations": ["PFE_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0020", "PFE_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0021"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Pfizer has received government inquiries and subpoenas and has incurred significant expense and fines in some instances; its 2018 Corporate Integrity Agreement expired in May 2023 and the OIG closed the matter in January 2025.", "citations": ["PFE_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0024"], "unverified": false}]}, {"ticker": "JNJ", "company": "Johnson & Johnson", "findings": [{"point": "The IRA subjects certain products to government-established pricing beginning in 2026, and failure to adhere to the government's interpretations pending litigation may expose J&J to penalties (10-K for fiscal 2025, ended December 28, 2025).", "citations": ["JNJ_10K_2025-12-28__risk_factors__0004"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "J&J says it faces significant regulatory scrutiny, and cGMP issues can lead to fines, recalls, shortages and delayed approvals.", "citations": ["JNJ_10K_2025-12-28__risk_factors__0007"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "The business section describes increasingly stringent regulation, including EU privacy/cyber laws and China data rules, and possible FDA civil or criminal penalties.", "citations": ["JNJ_10K_2025-12-28__business__0010", "JNJ_10K_2025-12-28__business__0012"], "unverified": false}]}, {"ticker": "MRK", "company": "Merck & Co Inc", "findings": [{"point": "Merck flags possible U.S. policy changes at HHS/FDA/CDC that could make approvals and vaccine recommendations harder, and notes FDA user fee elimination could delay inspections (10-K for fiscal 2024, ended December 31, 2024).", "citations": ["MRK_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0028"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Merck lists exposure to health care reform, FCPA, data privacy, local-manufacturing mandates and sustainability rules such as the EU's CSRD.", "citations": ["MRK_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0031"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Merck says it engages in public policy advocacy on cost containment and states its policies are consistent with EU directives, which it believes will not have a material effect.", "citations": ["MRK_10K_2024-12-31__business__0022", "MRK_10K_2024-12-31__business__0033"], "unverified": false}]}, {"ticker": "LLY", "company": "Eli Lilly and Company", "findings": [{"point": "Lilly cites risk from U.S. pricing agreements and policy efforts to align domestic prices with international benchmarks (10-K for fiscal 2025, ended December 31, 2025).", "citations": ["LLY_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0007"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Evolving regulatory priorities, cGMP scrutiny, and new compliance obligations may bring investigations, penalties and increased compliance costs.", "citations": ["LLY_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0037", "LLY_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0038"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Lilly makes substantial capital and operating investments in company-wide quality systems and controls to maintain cGMP compliance.", "citations": ["LLY_10K_2025-12-31__business__0074"], "unverified": false}]}, {"ticker": "ABBV", "company": "AbbVie Inc", "findings": [{"point": "AbbVie says it cannot guarantee ongoing regulatory compliance after approval, and possible actions include recalls, production shutdowns and market withdrawals (10-K for fiscal 2024, ended December 31, 2024).", "citations": ["ABBV_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0022"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Biologics are subject to regulations that are often more complex and extensive than those